        "title": "DspModSlot",
        "boxes": [
            {
                "box": {
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "text": "One mod slot, as the MSP `ModRouter`. It's polyphonic in `DspMod`, one voice per slot, so RNBO only generates its code once: every voice gets all five slots' settings, and the `switch`es pick this voice's. The source is scaled by the amount and goes out the destination's signal outlet (the voices' signals add up). On each note, the source's value (velocity, key, random, or the signal's current value) times the amount also goes out the destination's message outlet, for the destinations read once per note. Velocity, key and random hold their value until the next note.",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "id": "obj-1",
                    "patching_rect": [ 1070.0, 20.0, 460.0, 180.0 ],
                    "linecount": 9
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "maxclass": "newobj",
